00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:08.790
In other words, the authors here show how
to discard useless data points and train on

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.410
the important ones
and hereby they show how to push the power

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:19.730
law that describes model error and dataset
size to an exponential scaling!

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:25.790
In this video, we will explain different things
about this paper at a high-level how one can

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:32.450
move from a power law to exponential scaling
in theory, how much data one can discard in

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.450
practice,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:39.420
and how to define a metric that can help discard
useless data before training a neural network

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.060
(without using any data annotation!).

